1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
They just messed with the wrong Mexican.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Machete is a action, comedy, thriller film directed by Robert Rodriguez.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
After being set-up and betrayed by the man who hired him to assassinate a Texas Senator, an
ex-Federale launches a brutal rampage of revenge against his former boss.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Machete, played by Danny Trejo.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Luz, played by Michelle Rodriguez.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Sartana Rivera, played by Jessica Alba.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Senator John McLaughlin, played by Robert De Niro.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Rogelio Torrez, played by Steven Seagal.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Padre Cortez, played by Cheech Marin.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Machete (also known as Robert Rodriguez's Machete) is a 2010 American
exploitation action film directed by Robert Rodriguez and Ethan Maniquis.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The film is an expansion of a fake trailer published as a part of the promotion of
Rodriguez's and Quentin Tarantino's 2007 Grindhouse double-feature.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Machete continues the B movie and exploitation style of Grindhouse.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film stars Danny Trejo as the title character,
reprising the role from the fake trailer.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Trejo also previously portrayed an alternate version of
the character in the Spy Kids films.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film additionally co-stars Steven Seagal, Michelle Rodriguez, Jessica Alba,
Lindsay Lohan, Cheech Marin, Don Johnson and Robert De Niro.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It is Trejo's first lead role as the character, and Seagal's first theatrically released film
since 2002's Half Past Dead (and his last theatrically released film to date).

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Machete was released in the United States by 20th
Century Fox on September 3, 2010.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
A sequel, Machete Kills, solely directed by
Rodriguez, was released on October 11, 2013.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film explores themes of loss of loved one, illegal
immigration, border patrol, immigration law, machete.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and intense.
